# N1: the first attach of the COMBINED BEST on the AUDITED profile (c2-packed-tp4-best-gate: the gate-fcommit-quad profile with the
# five verify-glue levers and QWEN_FAST_TP4_VGLUE_AUDIT=1; the verify audits, the fused-commit audit and the singles audit on). An
# all-four reset, then the smoke of a warmup, one coding stream, the mixed four-stream test (concurrent4), the steady four-stream
# test (concurrent4_steady: a round of four fused publications under live banks) and steady_resend (a steady prompt's prefill after
# packed replays: the prefill-after-replay defect tp4/stack-fix removed). Nothing combined has run on a card before this job.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the four-card tp4/next window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it):
# copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/next and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here
# names a rig, a card or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The window's jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed
# from this branch.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG names the image N0 builds from this same commit; a later commit needs a new tag.
# C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-next-1 is a PLACEHOLDER: the driver of the window may substitute it (in every template) once the image is built
# from the pushed branch; the driver's IMAGE_TAG env overrides it.
# Duration (estimate): reset 1-3 min; the first engine build 10-30 min (cold kernel cache); the five tests 12-25 min: 30 / 50 / 100 min
# (a collective hang runs the 80-min ready loop, then the reset).
# Read: the ready line; the launched-argv line (profile c2-packed-tp4-best-gate; QWEN_FAST_TP=4 and the flags); no attach refusal;
# the '[PINDIAG] four-card prefill programs=' lines (the prefill tripwire: a program compiled after the warm); the fused-commit lines
# ('[PINDIAG] fused commit engaged', '[PACKED-FUSED] round=', the live-bank marker, the audit counts); the vglue lines ('[PINDIAG] tp4
# vglue engaged site=...' and every 'fell back' line); every audit line.
# STOP on an attach refusal, a hang, garbage text, an errored or empty stream, a prefill tripwire, a fused-commit audit or rule
# failure, a vglue audit mismatch or fell-back line. The smoke step (c2_smoke_check.py) enforces these; the coherence of the texts is
# read here.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-next-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-best-gate
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,coding,concurrent4,concurrent4_steady,steady_resend
